  (text "RS485 (replaces MAX485 module), fault-protected\nU701 THVD2410DR 3.3 V half-duplex transceiver on UART1: GPIO4 = TX (D), GPIO35 = RX (R),\nGPIO25 = DE + /RE (ESP-IDF UART RS485 half-duplex mode). A and B are rated +/-70 V and work over +/-25 V\ncommon mode, so a bus wire shorted to the 12 V or 24 V supply does no damage.\nR701 / R702 hold RX / TX high (R floats while transmitting); R703 holds DE low (receive) while the MCU is in reset.\nD701 / D702 SMAJ33CA clamp A and B to GND: 33 V standoff (above a 24 V system's 28.8 V), 53 V clamp (below 70 V).\nJ702 TERM: fit a shunt (120R across A-B) only on the two nodes at the ends of the bus.\nJ703 BIAS: fit both shunts, across 1-2 and 3-4 (A to 3V3 and B to GND via 330R), on exactly one node:\nidle A-B = 3.3 V x 60/(330+330+60) = 0.28 V with both ends terminated (receiver threshold 0.2 V).\nJumpers off = no termination and no bias. With J702/J703 fitted, a supply short burns R704-R706 (U701 survives)."
    (at 25.4 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "dcf36c07-7a63-499d-92a5-90f5e9e37df7")
  )
